  x invalid capability name `boot policy`
   ,-[tests/repos/broken-graph/components/base-image/fedora-bootc-44/manifest.kdl:6:23]
 5 | }
 6 | provides "rechunking" "boot policy" "selinux-policy"
   :                       ^^^^^^|^^^^^^
   :                             `-- lowercase, digits and dashes, starting with a letter
 7 | requires "bootc-base"
   `----
  help: a name is one or more segments joined by `/`, such as `rpm/dnf5`, and
        each segment starts with a lowercase letter

  x unknown base family `arch`
   ,-[tests/repos/broken-graph/components/core/three/manifest.kdl:5:1]
 4 | 
 5 | targets "arch"
   : ^^^|^^^
   :    `-- not a family this repository builds on
 6 | 
   `----
  help: known families: fedora, rhel, debian, ubuntu

  x two enabled components declare helper `shared.sh`
   ,-[tests/repos/broken-graph/components/core/two/manifest.kdl:7:1]
 6 | 
 7 | helpers "lib/two/shared.sh"
   : ^^^|^^^
   :    `-- mounted to the same path
 8 | provides {
   `----
  help: also declared by `core/one`; helper basenames must be unique across an
        image

  x `core/two` provides `rechunking`, which the base image already provides
    ,-[tests/repos/broken-graph/components/core/two/manifest.kdl:9:5]
  8 | provides {
  9 |     "rechunking"
    :     ^^^^^^|^^^^^
    :           `-- already provided by the base
 10 |     "shell-tools" exclusive=#true
    `----
  help: a component the base covers entirely is suppressed instead. This one
        also provides `shell-tools`, so its layer still builds and would
        provision `rechunking` a second time: split it, or drop the
        declaration

  x image `broken-graph` installs packages for `fedora`, but no enabled
  | component provides `build-environment` for that family
   ,-[tests/repos/broken-graph/image.kdl:3:1]
 2 | 
 3 | image {
   : ^^|^^
   :   `-- missing family adapter
 4 |     name "Broken Graph"
   `----

  x `core/three` does not support the `fedora` base family
  help: it declares support for: arch

  x `shell-tools` is provided by more than one enabled component
    ,-[tests/repos/broken-graph/components/core/two/manifest.kdl:10:5]
  9 |     "rechunking"
 10 |     "shell-tools" exclusive=#true
    :     ^^^^^^|^^^^^^
    :           `-- also provided elsewhere
 11 | }
    `----
  help: provided by: core/two, core/three. `core/two` declares it `exclusive`,
        so enable one provider

  x `quay.io/fedora/fedora-bootc:44` requires `bootc-base`, which nothing
